t-of-Foulkes vote behind Block, or the large undecided bloc breaks heavily against her, the margin could narrow considerably.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Dan McKee (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Rhode Island's governor's race is an open seat after Dan McKee lost the Democratic primary, and it has shaped up as one of the least competitive in the country. Helena Foulkes holds leads of twenty-plus points over Republican Aaron Guckian in every poll since June, with the latest surveys showing her at 41 to 45 percent in a field that includes independent Ken Block and two other minor candidates.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price a Foulkes win at roughly 97 percent. Guckian has run a troubled campaign, skipping a Rhode Island debate and resisting calls to withdraw in favor of Block, which splits the anti-Foulkes vote. The realistic question is the size of Foulkes' winning margin, not who wins, though a large undecided bloc and Block's appeal to change-minded voters leave modest room for tightening.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9964, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9941, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9927, "margin": 18.0}]}